# id: (hook line, explanation, fact/twist, comment q, source, hashtags)
D={
'chargers_i':("What if you never unplugged your chargers? 🔌 A lone phone charger with nothing attached uses almost no power.","But TVs, game consoles, cable boxes and other devices sitting on standby keep sipping electricity all day.","🤯 THE TWIST\nStandby or \"vampire\" power can add up to roughly 5–10% of a home's electricity use. A smart power strip makes it easy to cut it.","Do you unplug yours? Tell us in the comments!","U.S. Department of Energy, standby power","#shorts #howcome #energy #savemoney"),
'save5_i':("What if you saved $5 a day starting at age 20? 💰 That's about $1,825 a year.","If that money earned a hypothetical 7% average yearly return, compound interest could grow it to over $500,000 by age 65.","📌 NOTE\nThis is a math example, not financial advice. Real returns go up and down, and past results don't guarantee future ones.","Could you save $5 a day? Comment below!","compound interest calculation (hypothetical example)","#shorts #howcome #money #personalfinance"),
'minimum_i':("What if you only paid the minimum on your credit card? 💳 It feels safe because the monthly bill stays small.","But interest keeps adding up on the balance, so paying only the minimum can take years and cost much more than you borrowed.","🤯 THE TWIST\nIn the US, your card statement has to show a minimum payment warning: how long payoff takes and the total cost if you pay only the minimum.","Did you know about that box on your statement? Comment below!","CFPB, credit card minimum payment warning","#shorts #howcome #creditcard #money"),
'raise_i':("What if a raise made you take home LESS money? 🧾 Many people believe moving into a higher tax bracket taxes ALL their income at the higher rate.","US federal income tax brackets are marginal: only the dollars above each bracket line are taxed at the higher rate.","🤯 THE TWIST\nSo a raise still means more take-home pay from income tax alone. (Some benefit programs have separate income limits, so check your situation.)","Did you believe the tax bracket myth? Comment below!","IRS, federal income tax rates and brackets","#shorts #howcome #taxes #money"),
'voiceclone_i':("What if AI could clone your voice from just 3 seconds of audio? 🤖 Some AI voice tools can already copy a voice from a very short sample.","Scammers use cloned voices to fake calls from family members asking for money urgently.","🛡️ THE FIX\nAgree on a family safe word, and hang up and call back on a number you know if something feels off.","Would this fool you? Comment below!","FTC consumer alert on voice cloning scams","#shorts #howcome #AI #scams"),
'creditreport_i':("What if you never checked your credit report? 📉 A government study found about 1 in 5 people had an error on at least one of their credit reports.","Mistakes can lower your score without you noticing, which can affect loans, rent and more.","✅ GOOD NEWS\nIn the US you can check your reports from all three bureaus for free every week at AnnualCreditReport.com.","Ever checked yours? Comment below!","FTC study (2012); AnnualCreditReport.com","#shorts #howcome #creditscore #money"),
'emergency_i':("What if a surprise $400 bill showed up tomorrow? 💸 In a Federal Reserve survey, more than 1 in 3 US adults said they couldn't cover it with cash or its equivalent.","That's why many people build a small emergency fund, even a little each week.","📌 NOTE\nThis is general information, not financial advice.","Could you cover a surprise $400 bill? Comment below!","Federal Reserve, Economic Well-Being of U.S. Households (SHED)","#shorts #howcome #money #savings"),
'smishing_i':("What if you clicked every link in your text messages? 📱 Scam texts often pretend to be your bank or a package delivery.","One tap can lead to a fake site that steals your passwords or money.","🛡️ THE TRICK\nReal banks never ask you to send your login or verification code by text. When in doubt, open the official app yourself.","Have you gotten one of these texts? Comment below!","FTC, how to recognize and report spam text messages","#shorts #howcome #scams #cybersecurity"),
'update_i':("What if you never updated your phone? 📲 Updates feel annoying, so many people tap \"later\".","But most updates include security fixes for holes that hackers already know about.","🤯 THE TWIST\nSkipping updates leaves those known holes open. Turning on automatic updates is the easy fix.","Do you update right away? Comment below!","CISA, keep software up to date","#shorts #howcome #tech #cybersecurity"),
'location_i':("What if you shared your location all the time? 📍 Lots of apps track where you go, and some data brokers sell location data.","Check which apps really need your location in your phone settings.","🤯 THE SNEAKY PART\nPhotos can carry hidden GPS coordinates (metadata) that show exactly where they were taken, unless you turn location off for the camera.","Do you share your location? Comment below!","FTC actions on location data brokers; phone privacy settings","#shorts #howcome #privacy #tech"),
'wifi_i':("What if you used free public Wi-Fi for everything? 📶 Most websites today use encryption (HTTPS), which protects a lot.","But attackers can set up fake hotspots with names like \"Free Airport WiFi\" to trick people into connecting.","🛡️ TIP\nDouble-check the exact network name with staff, and avoid logging into sensitive accounts on networks you don't trust.","Do you use public Wi-Fi? Comment below!","FTC, are public Wi-Fi networks safe?","#shorts #howcome #wifi #cybersecurity"),
'overtime_i':("What if you worked 55 hours every week? ⏰ Long hours can feel productive.","But a WHO and ILO study linked working 55 or more hours a week with a higher risk of stroke and heart disease compared with 35–40 hours.","📌 NOTE\nThis is general information, not medical advice.","How many hours do you work a week? Comment below!","WHO/ILO, Environment International (2021)","#shorts #howcome #work #health"),
'emailnight_i':("What if you checked work emails every night? 📧 It can feel like getting ahead.","But late-night screens and work stress can make it harder to switch off and fall asleep.","🤯 THE TWIST\nFrance has a law (2017) giving many workers the \"right to disconnect\" from work messages after hours.","Do you check work emails at night? Comment below!","French Labor Code, right to disconnect (2017)","#shorts #howcome #work #sleep"),
'drowsy_i':("What if you drove after staying awake all night? 😵 You might feel fine.","But being awake for 24 hours can affect driving about like a blood alcohol level of 0.10%, which is above the legal limit in every US state.","🛡️ TIP\nIf you're too tired, don't drive. Rest first.","Ever driven while really tired? Comment below!","CDC, drowsy driving","#shorts #howcome #driving #sleep"),
'textdrive_i':("What if you texted while driving? 🚗 Reading a text takes your eyes off the road for about 5 seconds.","At 55 mph, that's like driving the length of a football field with your eyes closed.","🛡️ TIP\nPut your phone away or use do-not-disturb while driving.","Do you put your phone away when you drive? Comment below!","NHTSA, distracted driving","#shorts #howcome #driving #safety"),
'backup_i':("What if you never backed up your photos? 📸 If your phone breaks or gets lost, years of memories could vanish in a second.","Experts use the 3-2-1 rule: 3 copies of your data, on 2 kinds of storage, with 1 copy kept somewhere else (like the cloud).","✅ EASY START\nTurn on automatic cloud backup today.","When did you last back up your phone? Comment below!","CISA, data backup options (3-2-1 rule)","#shorts #howcome #tech #photos"),
'cash_i':("What if you kept all your money in cash at home? 💵 It can feel safe and easy.","But inflation slowly makes cash buy less every year, and cash at home can be lost in a fire or theft.","🤯 THE TWIST\nIn the US, deposits at FDIC-insured banks are insured up to $250,000 per depositor, per bank, per ownership category.","Cash or bank? Comment below!","FDIC, deposit insurance","#shorts #howcome #money #personalfinance"),
'speaker_i':("What if your smart speaker was always listening? 🔊 It does listen, but only for its wake word.","After it hears the wake word, it records your request and sends it to the cloud to process it.","🤯 THE TWIST\nYou can review and delete those voice recordings in the speaker's app, and many let you mute the microphone.","Do you have a smart speaker? Comment below!","Amazon Alexa and Google Assistant privacy settings","#shorts #howcome #tech #privacy"),
'bread_dyk':("Why does bread go stale? 🍞 Most people think it just dries out.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe starch inside slowly recrystallizes and hardens (starch retrogradation), even when the bread still has its water.","📌 FUN FACT\nThat's why bread goes stale faster in the fridge than on the counter. Freezing slows it down.","Toast or fresh bread? Comment below!","food science, starch retrogradation","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #food"),
'growl_dyk':("Why does your stomach growl? 🍽️ Most people think it only happens when you're hungry.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nYour gut squeezes and rumbles all the time to move food, gas and liquid along.","📌 WHY IT'S LOUDER\nWhen your stomach is empty, there's no food to muffle the sound, so the rumble is easier to hear.","Does your stomach growl in quiet rooms? Comment below!","gut motility basics (borborygmi)","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #body"),
'banana_dyk':("Why do bananas turn brown? 🍌 Ripe bananas release a gas called ethylene that speeds up ripening.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nIn the fridge, the peel turns black, but the fruit inside stays fresh longer.","📌 TIP\nKeep bananas away from other fruit if you don't want them to ripen too fast.","Green or spotty bananas? Comment below!","postharvest science, ethylene and ripening","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #food"),
'earspop_dyk':("Why do your ears pop on a plane? ✈️ When a plane climbs or lands, the air pressure around you changes fast.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe pop is a tiny tube (the Eustachian tube) opening to balance the pressure behind your eardrum.","📌 TIP\nYawning, swallowing or chewing gum helps it open.","Window or aisle seat? Comment below!","Mayo Clinic, airplane ear","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #travel"),
'salt_dyk':("Why does salt melt ice on roads? 🧂 Salt mixes with the thin layer of water on ice and lowers its freezing point.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nWhen it gets colder than about −10°C (around 15°F), regular rock salt barely works.","📌 FUN FACT\nThat's why road crews switch to other chemicals or sand in extreme cold.","Snow or sunshine? Comment below!","freezing point depression; road salt guidance","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #winter"),
'microwave_dyk':("Why do microwaves heat food unevenly? 🍲 Microwaves bounce around inside and create hot and cold spots. That's why the plate spins.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nMicrowaves don't cook from the inside out. They mostly heat the outer layer first, and the heat spreads inward.","📌 TIP\nStir halfway and let food stand a minute so the heat evens out.","Do you stir your food? Comment below!","FDA, microwave oven radiation","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #kitchen"),
'foot_dyk':("Why does your foot fall asleep? 🦶 Sitting on it squeezes the nerves and blood flow, so signals can't get through.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe pins-and-needles feeling is your nerves waking back up and firing all at once.","📌 NOTE\nIt's usually harmless and passes quickly. If it happens often for no reason, talk to a doctor.","Does this happen to you? Comment below!","Cleveland Clinic, paresthesia","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #body"),
'leaves_dyk':("Why do leaves change color in fall? 🍂 Leaves are green because of chlorophyll, which helps them make food from sunlight.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe yellow and orange colors were in the leaves all summer. When the chlorophyll breaks down in fall, they finally show.","📌 FUN FACT\nThe reds come from new pigments made in autumn.","Fall or spring? Comment below!","USDA Forest Service, why leaves change color","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #nature"),
'battery_dyk':("Why do batteries die faster in the cold? 🔋 The chemical reactions inside slow down when it's freezing, so less power comes out.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe energy isn't gone. Warm the battery back up, and much of it comes back.","📌 TIP\nKeep your phone in an inside pocket on cold days.","Has your phone died in the cold? Comment below!","Battery University, cold temperature effects","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #tech"),
'spoon_dyk':("Why does a spoon look bent in water? 🥄 Light changes direction when it moves from water into air (refraction).","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nLight travels about 25% slower in water than in air, and that change in speed is what bends it.","📌 FUN FACT\nThe same effect makes pools look shallower than they really are.","Did you try this as a kid? Comment below!","physics of refraction (water refractive index ≈ 1.33)","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #physics"),
'carfog_dyk':("Why do car windows fog up? 🚗 Warm, damp air from your breath hits the cold glass and turns into tiny water drops.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nTurning on the air conditioning helps, even in winter, because it dries the air.","📌 TIP\nUse the defrost setting with A/C on, and fresh air instead of recirculate.","Do you use this trick? Comment below!","AAA and automotive defogging guidance","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #cars"),
'helium_dyk':("Why does helium make your voice squeaky? 🎈 Most people think your vocal cords vibrate faster.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nYour vocal cords stay the same. Sound travels almost 3 times faster in helium, which changes the tone (timbre) of your voice.","⚠️ SAFETY\nNever inhale helium straight from a tank; it can be dangerous.","Have you tried it? Comment below!","physics of sound in gases","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #physics"),
'mosquito_dyk':("Why do mosquito bites itch? 🦟 When a mosquito bites, it injects saliva to keep your blood flowing.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe itch isn't the bite itself. It's your immune system reacting to that saliva and releasing histamine.","📌 TIP\nDon't scratch; a cold pack can help.","Do mosquitoes love you? Comment below!","CDC and Mayo Clinic, mosquito bites","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #body"),
'moon_dyk':("Why does the moon look bigger near the horizon? 🌕 Most people think it's closer.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nIt's not bigger at all. Take a photo and it's the same size. It's an illusion your brain creates (the moon illusion).","📌 FUN FACT\nThe moon is actually slightly farther away from you when it's on the horizon.","Have you noticed this? Comment below!","NASA, the moon illusion","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #space"),
'pencap_dyk':("Why do pen caps have a tiny hole? 🖊️ Most people think it stops the ink from drying out.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThe hole is a safety feature: if a child swallows the cap, air can still pass through.","📌 NOTE\nIt reduces risk but doesn't remove it, so keep small parts away from kids.","Do you chew on pen caps? Comment below!","BIC, pen cap safety","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #design"),
'toast_dyk':("Why does toast land butter side down? 🍞 It's not bad luck.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nA physicist found that from normal table height, toast only has time to flip about half a turn before it hits the floor.","📌 FUN FACT\nFrom a much taller table, it would have time to land butter side up more often.","Has this happened to you? Comment below!","Robert Matthews, European Journal of Physics (1995)","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #physics"),
'foil_dyk':("Why is foil shiny on one side? ✨ Many think the shiny side is for cooking.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nIt's just how it's made: two sheets are rolled together at the end, and the sides touching the polished rollers come out shiny.","📌 FUN FACT\nFor regular foil, both sides cook the same.","Which side do you use? Comment below!","Reynolds Kitchens, shiny vs dull side","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #kitchen"),
'glue_dyk':("Why doesn't glue stick inside the bottle? 🧴 White glue needs air to dry. In a closed bottle, the water can't evaporate.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nSuper glue is different: it hardens with tiny amounts of moisture, like the moisture on your skin.","📌 TIP\nThat's why super glue bonds fingers so fast. Be careful!","Have you ever glued your fingers? Comment below!","cyanoacrylate adhesive chemistry","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #chemistry"),
'shiver_dyk':("Why do we shiver when we're cold? 🥶 Your muscles start shaking fast, all on their own.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nThose tiny shakes are your body making heat. Shivering can boost your body's heat production several times over.","📌 FUN FACT\nIt's an automatic reflex controlled by your brain.","Cold or hot weather? Comment below!","human thermoregulation physiology","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #body"),
'books_dyk':("Why do old books smell so good? 📚 As paper ages, chemicals inside it slowly break down.","🤯 THE SURPRISING PART\nOne of them is vanillin, the same compound that gives vanilla its sweet smell.","📌 FUN FACT\nScientists have even studied old-book smell to judge how paper is aging.","Do you love that smell? Comment below!","Strlic et al., Analytical Chemistry (2009)","#shorts #DidYouKnow #science #books"),
}
def text(k):
    h,a,b,q,s,tags=D[k]
    sub='🔔 Subscribe to HOWCOME? for more \"What if...?\" questions about everyday life!' if k.endswith('_i') else '🔔 Subscribe to Did You Know Official for the science behind everyday things!'
    disc='\n\n⚠️ For education only, not financial, legal or medical advice.' if k.endswith('_i') else ''
    return f"{h}\n\n{a}\n\n{b}\n\n💬 {q}\n\n📚 SOURCE: {s}{disc}\n{sub}\n\n{tags}"
